<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andhra State</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1953–1956</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andhra State was a state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> formed on 1 October 1953 from the Telugu-speaking northern districts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madras-state">Madras State</a>, with its capital at Kurnool. It was the first Indian state created on linguistic lines, after the death of Potti Sriramulu during a hunger strike for it in 1952. On 1 November 1956 it merged with the Telugu-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a> region of Hyderabad State to form <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andhra-state.jpg" alt="Andhra State" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Furfur · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andhra-India_1953.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
